If $f(x, y, z)$ is constant, then
$
  0 = dif f
    = ((∂ f)/(∂ x))_(y, z) dif x
      + ((∂ f)/(∂ y))_(x, z) dif y
      + ((∂ f)/(∂ z))_(x, y) dif z.
$
The variables $x, y, z$ cannot be varied independently on the surface. Holding $y$ fixed,
$
  0
    = ((∂ f)/(∂ x))_(y, z)
      + ((∂ f)/(∂ z))_(x, y) ((∂ z)/(∂ x))_y,
$
so
$ ((∂ z)/(∂ x))_y = - ((∂ f)/(∂ x))_(y, z) / ((∂ f)/(∂ z))_(x, y). $
The same argument yields $((∂ x)/(∂ y))_z$ and $((∂ y)/(∂ z))_x$, and the product of the three ratios is $-1$.
